FLAGS['DKA-19'] = "Card d ‘large fluid volumes’: PECARN FLUID (2018, 1389 episodes) found no difference in altered mental status or cerebral injury with faster vs slower fluids or 0.9% vs 0.45% saline, so this risk factor is weaker than stated. Card-layer line ‘0.5–1%, mortality up to 25%’ is close to ISPAD 2022 (0.5–0.9%, 21–24%). DocT keys cerebral oedema as the main adult HHS risk; best of the options offered but rare in adults (under 0.1%)."
FLAGS['DKA-21'] = "DocT GT key (glucose 240 = euglycaemic DKA) and its qpack note follow the old 250 cut-off; by the 2024 definition (<200) glucose 240 is ordinary DKA. The answer stands only because plain DKA is not an option."
FLAGS['DKA-22'] = "Card a ‘more common than DKA’ is Marrow’s statement; most texts call DKA commoner, and 2024 US data show similar shares (DKA 38%, HHS 35%, mixed 27%). Card watch line already notes the disagreement."
